1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
One turn. A new possibility. Learn it here. Try it in your hands.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Start with one small step. You do not need to know how to solve yet. START HERE. No account needed. Pause whenever you want to try a step.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Find your starting point. Or join a lesson if you already know where to begin.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Choose your current level. Pick what you can do on your own today. FIND YOUR ROUTE. This is a recommendation, not a test. You can change routes later.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Choose a way of thinking. Layers and pairs, or blocks and the middle slice?

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Be honest about your foundation. Roux routes are included when they fit your experience.

7
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Choose a goal. Here, we want a first independent solve.

8
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Choose your practice habits. Short sessions count. At the club, at home, or both.

9
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Read the reason for your route. This example starts with LBL. Open the first lesson when ready.

10
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:57,000
Match the starting hold. Here: white on top, green in front. MEET THE MOVES. Read direction while looking straight at the face being turned.

11
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:02,000
U / D: up / down. L / R: left / right. F / B: front / back.

12
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Plain letter: clockwise 90°. A prime mark reverses it. A 2 means a half turn.

13
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Choose U′, then Direction view. Look straight at the upper face to judge its direction.

14
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Play the move. Watch the top layer, then copy it on your cube.

15
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:26,000
Replay, or return to Holding view. Changing the camera changes your view, not the cube.

16
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Build a white daisy. Put white petals around the yellow centre first. LEARN ONE STAGE. Prepared lesson example: set up your physical cube before copying its moves.

17
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:38,000
Use the example setup. Open “Follow along with a physical cube”.

18
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Apply its scramble from solved. Start white-up, green-front. Pause the video to prepare.

19
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Return to the player. Read Observe, Prepare and Check the result.

20
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Try Next move. Copy one turn, then check what changed.

21
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Follow whole-cube rotations too. A shown x, y or z is a real regrip. Camera dragging is only a view change.

22
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:09,000
Start with a method you know. Choose LBL while learning your first independent solve. SOLVE YOUR CUBE. Prepared input example. The solution shown comes from the entered scramble.

23
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:15,000
Paste the scramble you used. Only use this option if that sequence was applied from solved.

24
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:21,000
Choose Explain with LBL. The site checks and builds your teaching steps.

25
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:27,000
Follow the solution player. Match the holding, then use Next move.

26
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Keep the physical cube in sync. A stage jump changes the display; it does not turn your cube.

27
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:37,000
Choose Enter colors. Follow the holding diagram for the current face. ENTER COLOURS. Input demonstration: this clip does not complete all six faces.

28
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:42,000
Pick a colour, then a sticker. Centres are fixed. Copy your actual cube.

29
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Continue through all six faces. Keep the top and front directions shown for each face.

30
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Review and Check colors. Finish every face and correct errors before solving.

31
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Try to name the case. Study the diagram before you reveal the answer. FORMULA PRACTICE. CFOP practice is useful once you have learned the corresponding method.

32
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Show the solution. Check the holding and formula. Repeat when it feels familiar.

33
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:06,000
Scramble from solved. Start white-up, green-front and apply the printed moves. TIME YOUR PRACTICE. Timer control demonstration only. The short run shown is not a real solve.

34
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:12,000
Check the six-face diagram. Compare its stickers with your cube.

35
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:17,000
Hold Space until Ready. Release to start the timer.

36
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:23,000
Press again to stop. On a touch screen: hold, release, then tap to stop.

37
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:30,000
Inspection is optional. Use the checkbox when you want inspection before timing.

38
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:36,000
Review your times and averages. ao5 and ao12 summarize five and twelve solves. YOUR PROGRESS. Sample records, not member results. History stays in this browser on this device.

39
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:42,000
Correct a result when needed. Use +2 for a penalty or DNF for an unfinished solve.

40
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:48,000
Export a backup. Keep CSV or JSON before clearing data or changing devices.

41
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:54,000
Roux builds two side blocks. It uses the middle slice instead of treating every layer separately. ANOTHER WAY TO THINK. Advanced Roux is Preview. Start with Beginner Roux if these ideas are new.

42
00:03:54,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Read the setup and block check. Different pieces can suggest a square, a pair, or another construction.

43
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:04,000
Try one explained example. Follow the shown hold. M and M′ turn the middle slice.

44
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:08,000
Progress at your own pace. The lessons and CMLL library explain the next stages.

45
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:14,000
Lab explores candidate routes. It can compare white or yellow bottoms and different left colours. ROUX LAB · EXPERIMENTAL. Search completed before this shot. Real verified route; original playback speed.

46
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:20,000
Read the recommendation carefully. Move counts and handling scores are references, not promises of speed.

47
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:26,000
Follow the selected route. Use the player, then compare it with another on a physical cube.

48
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:32,000
Keep notes about the feel. Trials help compare the same starting cube. Your records stay local.

49
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:38,000
Open Guide and pick a chapter. Find the instructions for the page you are using. HELP WHEN YOU NEED IT. Open Guide from the club navigation. Tours can be skipped or exited at any time.

50
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:44,000
Expand Every control, explained. Look up a button without replaying the whole video.

51
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:50,000
Try a page tour if you need it. Choose one thing to practise today, then try it with your cube.

52
00:04:50,000 --> 00:05:00,000
Your turn. Keep your curiosity. Learn it here. Try it in your hands. Full guide: open Guide.
